Let the initial position of the projectile is $y_0 = 0$ (since the projectile is launched from the ground).
Let the time taken to reach maximum height is $t_0$.
At the maximum height, the final velocity is $v_f = 0$.

We can use the kinematic equation:
$v_f = v_0 -gt$
$0 = 20 - 9.8t_0$
$9.8t_0 = 20$
$t_0 = \frac{20}{9.8} \approx 2.02125 \text{ s}$

