$v_2^2 = v_0^2 - 2gt(y_f - y_0)$
Where $v_2$ is the final velocity, $v_0$ is the initial velocity, $g$ is the acceleration acceleration, $t$ is the time, and $v_2$ is the final velocity.
At the maximum height, $v_2 = 0$.
So, $0^2 = (20)^2 - 2(9.8)t_0(y_f - 0)$
$0 = 400 - 19.6t_0 v_0$
