Lattice energy (U) = -A * (1 - 1/n) * (Q1 * Q2 / r)

Where:
A = Born-Lande equation constant = 2.21 x 10^-19 J nm
n = Born exponent (typically between 5 and 12, we will use 9 as an approximation for ionic compounds)
Q1 = charge of ion 1 (Ca2+) = +2
Q2 = charge of ion 2 (Cl-) = -1
r = distance between ions = 0.231 nm

Now, we can plug in the values into the equation:

