\]
\[
\frac{1}{T_2} - \frac{1}{T_1} = 0.0012 - 0.0018 = -0.0006 \, \text{K}^{-1}.
\]
Rearranging the Arrhenius equation to solve for \( E_a \):
\[
E_a = -R \left( \frac{\ln(k_{f2}/k_{f1})}{1/T_2 - 1/T_1} \right) = -2 \, \text{cal K}^{-1} \text{mol}^{-1} \left( \frac{11.513}{-0.0006} \right).
\]
Calculating \( E_a \):
\[
E_a \approx 2 \times \frac{11.513}{0.0006} \approx 38,377 \, \text{cal mol}^{-1} \approx 38 \, \text{kcal mol}^{-1}.
\]
Thus, the activation energy is:
\[
\boxed{38 \, \text{kcal mol}^{-1}}.
\]
